@@ -422,9 +422,38 @@ later card had already earned can disappear.
 
 ### `GET /players/:playerId/record?asOf=YYYY-MM-DD`
 `asOf` is required. Answers `playerId`, `clubId`, `asOf`, `cards`, `yellows`, `reds`, `points`,
-`finesPence`, `matchesBanned`, `standing`.
+`finesPence`, `matchesBanned`, `matchesServed`, `matchesOutstanding`, `standing`.
 
-`standing` is `suspended` when anything is being served, `warned` from 3 points, else `clear`.
+`standing` is `suspended` while any match remains outstanding as of `asOf`, `warned` from 3 points,
+else `clear`.
+
+### `GET /players/:playerId/suspensions?asOf=YYYY-MM-DD`
+`asOf` is required. Answers `playerId`, `asOf`, `matchesBanned`, `matchesServed`,
+`matchesOutstanding`, `suspended` and `entries`, oldest first.
+
+Each entry carries `cardId`, `fixtureId`, `teamId`, `shownOn`, `matches`, `served`, `outstanding`,
+`servedIn` (fixture ids in serving order) and `clearedOn` (the day its last match was served, else
+`null`).
+
+Only cards that carry a ban appear in `entries`. A ban is served over games of the side the card was
+shown for; only `played` fixtures serve anything. Each played game serves one match off the earliest
+outstanding card shown to that side before it (strictly: the game where the card was shown does not
+count). Rescinded cards drop out and any games they had consumed fall through to later cards.
+
+While any match remains outstanding the player is barred from every side of their current club. A
+transfer moves the bar to the new club; the serving games stay tied to the old team.
+
+Both routes need a bearer token, take no other query field, and treat days and unknown ids like
+other readings.
+
+### `GET /fixtures/:fixtureId/eligibility`
+No query parameters. Answers `fixtureId`, `playedOn`, `asOf` (the day before the game) and
+`ineligible`: every registered player at either club who has a match outstanding as of `asOf`, home
+side first then by player id.
+
+Each entry carries `playerId`, `clubId`, `teamId` (their side in this game) and `outstanding`.
+
+Needs a bearer token and treats unknown ids like other readings.
 
 ---
 
